Before, this was silently overwritten so it was "okay" but now with the new brewing fix moving generation to use the mod id instead of minecraft's namespace, running datagen creates duplicate brewing recipes for all vanilla potions used as a base.

As an example, in my mod Lost Relics I have a recipe that follows;
```java
private static class LostRelicsBrewingProvider extends FabricBrewingProvider {
		protected LostRelicsBrewingProvider(RecipeOutput output) {
			super(output);
		}

		@Override
		protected void buildMixes() {
			buildMix(Potions.AWKWARD, LostRelicsItems.TAINTED_BLOOD_CRYSTAL, LostRelicsPotions.TAINTED);
		}
	}
```

and the resulting generation includes recipes for turning vanilla Awkward potions into splash and lingering potions, creating duplicate recipes that used to be silently overwritten.

